From 06a51eef19128759d24ad9a03b3c64ea99c5bf0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sm64ds-3ds <244728604+ethanseagull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 14:29:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] ntr, hal: cheaper per-pixel passes and divides on the
 3DS port

Measured with a sampling profile of Bob-omb Battlefield in Azahar (the
3DS's ARM11 has no divide instruction and pays for every branch):
- io.cpp run_divide: a 32-bit divide when both operands fit, and the
  remainder from the quotient (it did two 64-bit library divides on
  every write to the unit, ~9% of the frame).
- message_compositor.cpp: window_mask_row fills a line's window mask as
  spans (SM64DS_WINROW_VERIFY=1 checks it against window_mask); the BG
  loop, hide_3d_outside_windows and bm_fill_default use it, and
  bm_fill_default reads BLDCNT once per pass instead of per pixel and
  maps host columns through a table instead of a divide. g_a_clean[y]
  marks rows with no hit, so the clear, the blit and the lift scan skip
  them; every writer of a hit resets it.
- ppu_sub.cpp ppu_compose_stacked: the source column from a table, not
  a divide per pixel.
Same answers throughout. Azahar, Bob-omb Battlefield: engine A's
compose 44.5 -> 17.7 ms a frame; ten-level sweep 10/10, every tick down.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
